c256x2048 t=8 contention round — 2026-08-11, branch perf/c256-contention @ 668f5ec
base main @ dcc9395 (PR #503 merged: the derived rows-per-block rule is the default)
=====================================================================================
VERDICT  Both levers the round was opened for are REFUTED. Nothing ships.
         Full write-up: docs/C256_CONTENTION.md.
         L1 (a FINER shard block than the block-count rule can reach): null at
            one shift finer, then monotone adverse — 0.9947 / 1.0221 / 1.1179 /
            1.2026 / 1.2106 at -1/-2/-3/-4/-5 shifts against a pinned identity
            control. Wide path never reached at ANY rung, so the lever was not
            killed by its counter-force; it is killed by shard-line footprint.
         L2 (the shard lock's waiting policy, four arms): every arm inside a
            +-1.8% identity-control band. Priced first: the whole waiting
            population is 1.20 CPU ms/frame = 10.7% of the tracker's 11.23, so
            a PERFECT lock was worth 2.378x -> 2.265x against a 1.4x bar.

Box     Apple M4 Pro, 8P+4E, macOS 26.5.2, aarch64. Every timed run under
        `measlock`. Builds and gates NICED; timed runs never.
        Idle: foreign_max = 0 on the shift ladder and the thread-count ladder,
        1 on the n=15 lock settle, 1-2 on the cross-cell relax grid (LOAD-TAGGED
        there: paired ratios hold, absolute ms/frame are inflated ~4%).
Build   cargo --release, no target-cpu=native. Arms copied to names cargo never
        writes (scripts/perf/c256_build.sh) so a later build cannot swap an
        inode under a running measurement.
Vector  ~/tmp/bpsrows/vec/C256x2048_420_8b__t8.avif + the matching IVF
        (mk_shardsize_vectors.sh; a centred 1:1 crop, 4x2 = 8 tiles, 8-bit
        4:2:0, all-intra). Companions: C1024x{192,384,576}, C3840x256,
        v4k_8tile. Every IVF is N repeats of the SAME key-frame OBU the AVIF
        carries, so our arm and dav1d decode identical work.
Fit     two-point `total = a + b*frames`, n_lo/n_hi per cell and never past the
        stream length (22/225 at c256x2048). ROUND 0 DISCARDED (first touch of
        each (arm, cell) is cold). Ratios PAIRED per round, then median; bands
        are min/max over rounds; `sign` = rounds on the same side of 1.000.
Ident   Every timed arm's CHECKSUM equals dav1d 1.5.4's md5 at t=1 AND t=8
        (248f00770bd2f196fad95684c47954f0), 15 arms, taken BEFORE any timing.

