TWO INSTRUMENT TRAPS, BOTH HIT AND BOTH RECORDED
  1. A NICED counted run measures a different machine. On Darwin `nice -n 19`
     maps to background QoS and lands all eight workers on the four E-cores.
     Registration COUNTS are indifferent; CONTENTION counts are not — the first
     pass read lockslow = 1,072/frame where the un-niced build reads 96.
     scripts/perf/c256_contention.sh runs UN-NICED under measlock for this
     reason even though it only reports counters.
  2. The counter and the profile disagreed by ~150x on `TinyLock::lock_slow`,
     and both are right. `core::hint::spin_loop()` was directly measured at
     7.6 ns per iteration on an idle core, 6.7 ns of which is the hint (200M x 3
     rounds minus an empty-loop control; examples/spin_cost.rs reproduces the
     hint at 6.78 ns under load), which over 1,007-1,373 counted
     iterations/frame predicts 0.008-0.010 CPU ms/frame
     against a profile reading 0.86-1.20. Reconciled by running BOTH instruments
     in ONE binary (probe-wide + sample, 9,000 frames): 5,984 leaf samples
     against that run's own 1,373 spins/frame over 6,949 windowed frames =
     ~627 ns per iteration under real contention. `lock_slow` is 32 bytes of
     text (nm: 0x1001b70fc..0x1001b711c) and `add_contended` is a separate
     symbol with 499 samples, so it is not misattribution to a neighbour.

1. THE RESIDUAL, MEASURED (c256x2048, n=7, idle; regs from probe-sites, lost=0)
   t   ours   untrk  dav1d  ours/dav  ceil   trkCPU ms/f  regs/frame  ns/reg  cores
   1  12.404  11.827  9.442    1.314  1.253       0.596     272,505    2.19   1.00
   2   7.444   6.144  4.833    1.540  1.271       2.578     569,690    4.52   1.98
   4   4.590   3.236  2.535    1.811  1.277       5.229     569,690    9.18   3.87
   8   3.764   2.099  1.576    2.387  1.331      11.227     569,690   19.71   6.70
   The registration count is IDENTICAL at t=2/4/8 (the tile_threading latch is
   already thrown at t=2) and the cost per registration DOUBLES with every
   doubling of workers. At most 10.7% of it is waiting. So >=89% of the
   tracker's t=8 cost is the UNCONTENDED path getting slower as more cores touch
   the same shard — roughly one cross-core transfer of the shard's own cache
   line per registration.

2. SELF TIME (sample, 30 s, busy-normalised; parked threads bucketed as idle)
   arm         busy    idle%  entropy kernels    lf   cdef tracker   sync runtime other
   plain t=2  45,301   34.23    56.11   12.37  7.40   3.56   13.38   0.26    2.97  3.95
   plain t=8 136,724   25.33    44.92   11.11  5.14   2.22   22.91   4.75    3.39  5.57
   relax t=8 137,723   24.70    44.74   11.02  5.26   2.27   23.26   4.77    3.32  5.36
   park  t=8 129,474   28.97    47.41   11.67  5.23   2.32   25.16   0.69    3.28  4.24
   The park arm converts the spin into idle (sync 4.75 -> 0.69, idle 25.3 ->
   29.0) and moves neither wall (0.9922) nor CPU (1.0002): the waiting is real,
   removable as CPU, and not on the critical path.

3. THE CONTENTION CENSUS (per frame, un-niced, median of 5 reps)
   arm      contended  lockslow  spins  spins/wait      (569,690 regs/frame)
   plain        1,506        99  1,007       10.16      contended = 0.264% of regs
   backoff      1,545        98    756        7.69
   relax        1,457        90    216        2.40      4.7x fewer iterations, live
   yield        1,492        74    108        1.47
   park         1,801     1,644      0        0.00      (counts every contended lock)
   w_shards / w_blocks / w_full are 0 at EVERY rung of the pin ladder, including
   shift 6 on both planes — the wide path is never reached on this cell.

NOT COVERED
   x86_64 (where every lock acquisition is dearer — a waiting-policy arm could
   behave differently and this round says nothing about it), wasm32, 10-bit,
   12-bit, 4:4:4, film grain, inter/video content, `unchecked`, `asm`, t=16.
   One vector, one content class, one box. Loop restoration executes zero blocks
   here. The shift ladder was swept on a per-plane PIN, not on a candidate
   shipping rule — this round only establishes there is nothing to win on this
   cell, so no refining rule was designed. SLOTS untouched; no reservation
   widened anywhere; no tile- or worker-keyed scheme built.
